                <div class="post-article__text">
                    <div class="post_details_wrapper">
                        <div class="post_details">
                            <p class="this_article"><strong>In this article:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><a href="#">What Is LED Light Therapy?</a></li>
                                <li><a href="#">How LED light therapy works</a></li>
                                <li><a href="#">Benefits of LED Light Therapy</a></li>
                                <li><a href="#">How to Prepare</a></li>
                                <li><a href="#">LED Light Therapy vs. Microneedling</a></li>
                                <li><a href="#">At-Home vs. In Clinic</a></li>
                                <li><a href="#">Are At-Home LED devices safe?</a></li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="growing_post pt-40">
                                <p>Growing in popularity over the last few years, LED light therapy promises to fight
                                    acne and signs of aging with the use of light technology. Pair this with the funky
                                    device that will make you look like you’re futuristic in the year 2165, and you have
                                    the beauty treatment every beauty lover is desperate to try.</p>
                                <p>Here you are probably wondering how exactly can a device that emits bright LED lights
                                    aid to have a clearer and brighter complexion? Better yet, transform your skin?</p>
                                <p>If you are frustrated by things like wrinkling, sagging skin, acne and inflammation.
                                    LED light therapy is a must try for you! The beauty devices have been used by our
                                    favourite celebrities like Kourtney Kardashian and Jessica Alba. You’d have to agree
                                    when we say that innovative beauty products are so much more fun. We thought we’d
                                    give you the rundown on everything you need to know about LED light therapy. What it
                                    is, how it works, and any other must-know information about this life changing skin
                                    treatment.</p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="what_led pt-40">
                                <p class="fs-24"><strong>What is LED light therapy?</strong></p>
                                <p>LED means light-emitting diode. LED light therapy is a noninvasive approach that
                                    works by emitting infrared lights in different wavelengths/spectrums, which have
                                    distinct skincare benefits. Red light is the most frequently used light to promote
                                    circulation. Blue light kills bacteria.</p>
                                <p>During an LED light therapy at-home treatment, the device sends light waves deep into
                                    the skin to trigger natural intracellular reactions. Depending on which light is
                                    being used, the skin will respond differently. Using the red light, your skin
                                    responds by building, strengthening and maximizing cellular structure. Red light is
                                    additionally believed to target oil glands and reduce cytokines, which are
                                    responsible for inflammation and play a role in chronic acne. If you opt to use the
                                    blue light, specific wavelengths stimulate production of oxygen radicals that kill
                                    P.acnes bacteria.</p>
                                <p>And, all of this is done without damaging the skin.</p>
                            </div>
                            <figure class="inline-promo-card">
                                <picture>
                                    <source media="(min-width:768px)" srcset="assets/images/blogs/discover_best_seller.webp">
                                    <img src="assets/images/blogs/discover_best_seller_mob.webp" alt="">
                                </picture>
                                <figcaption>
                                    Discover our Best Sellers
                                    <a href="#" class="btn btn--primary-white" >Shop Now</a>
                                </figcaption>
                            </figure>
                            <div class="how_led_works pt-30 pt-md-60">
                                <p class="fs-24"><strong>How LED light therapy works</strong></p>
                                <p>At home LED light therapy devices have been created so you can treat skin problems at
                                    home on your own. The light doesn’t cause any burns or skin damage, it is painless
                                    with no down time.</p>
                                <p>LED light therapy harnesses the healing power of light for complete skin
                                    rejuvenation. LED light therapy works on a cellular level to tackle a huge range of
                                    skin concerns. It is really quite incredible!</p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="epidermis pt-30 pt-md-60">
                                <img src="assets/images/blogs/epidermis.webp" alt="" class="img-fluid">
                            </div>
                            <div class="benefits_of_led pt-30 pt-md-60">
                                <p class="fs-24"><strong>What are the benefits of LED light therapy?</strong></p>
                                <p>People are turning to LED light therapy to fix skin problems such as acne. In fact,
                                    it works well for a variety of skin conditions, from eczema, to rosacea, and so much
                                    more.</p>
                                <p>Light therapy has an extensive list of amazing benefits such as;</p>
                                <ul>
                                    <li>Stimulates collagen production</li>
                                    <li>Smooths fine lines and wrinkles</li>
                                    <li>Reduces redness and inflammation</li>
                                    <li>Prevents breakouts by killing the acne-causing bacteria</li>
                                    <li>Minimizes pores by regulating oil production</li>
                                    <li>Improves appearance of scarring by promoting skin cell healing</li>
                                    <li>Brightens skin and dark spots</li>
                                    <li>Smooths skin texture</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                            <div class="how_to_prepare pt-30 pt-md-60">
                                <p class="fs-24"><strong>How to Prepare for LED Light Therapy</strong></p>
                                <p>It’s always recommended that the skin must be cleansed and clean without any make up
                                    before LED light therapy treatment. For in-clinic treatments you will be required to
                                    wear protective eyewear to protect your eyes from the light.</p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="c-subscribe-form">
                                <p>Get the latest from Qure</p>
                                <form>
                                    <input type="email" placeholder="Your Email" />
                                    <button>{{> e-icon icon="arrow"}}</button>
                                </form>
                            </div>
                            <div class="led_vs_microneedling">
                                <p class="fs-24"><strong>LED Light Therapy vs. Microneedling</strong></p>
                                <p>Micro-needling is another popular facial treatment to rejuvenate the skin. It can
                                    improve signs of ageing, acne, scarring and pigmentation.</p>
                                <p>The needles create microscopic wounds on the top layer of the skin and ignite the
                                    body’s natural defence is to repair the wounds, causing collagen regeneration to
                                    create new tissue and the result is a fresher, younger looking appearance.</p>
                                <p>The benefits are the same as LED light therapy, but a little more invasive.</p>
                                <p>Often facial treatment in-clinics include the combination of LED light and
                                    microneedling in one visit to effectively treat multiple skin concerns. The treated
                                    skin is exposed to LED light therapy after micro-needling or microdermabrasion to
                                    maximise results. LED light is clinically proven to stimulate cellular activity,
                                    therefore encouraging collagen production. LED light therapy will further reduce
                                    fine lines and wrinkles , improve scarring, clear blemishes, improve skin tone, and
                                    repair sun damage. Some experts might label this combination as the “perfect
                                    pair”.</p>
                            </div>
                            <figure class="inline-promo-card">
                                <picture>
                                    <source media="(min-width:768px)" srcset="assets/images/blogs/skin_journey.webp">
                                    <img src="assets/images/blogs/skin_journey_mob.webp" alt="">
                                </picture>
                                <figcaption>
                                    Learn more and share <br> your skincare journey
                                    <a href="#" class="btn btn--primary-white" >Join Our VIP Community</a>
                                </figcaption>
                            </figure>
                            <div class="home_vs_clinic pt-30 pt-md-60">
                                <p class="fs-24"><strong>At-Home vs. In Clinic</strong></p>
                                <p>Research and clinical studies have proven that LED light therapy treatments can
                                    effectively treat a multitude of skin concerns and provide transformative results.
                                    But the results are cumulative, meaning you won’t see long-term benefits from that
                                    single salon trip you treat yourself to every so often.</p>
                                <p>In order to see long-term results then regular appointments are required, and these
                                    regular in-clinic trips are not only time consuming, but can be very expensive. If
                                    regular appointments aren’t an option, investing in a good quality at-home LED light
                                    therapy device could be the answer.</p>
                                <p>Though in-clinic LED panels are more powerful than at-home devices, it doesn't mean
                                    an at-home device won't be effective or offer the same benefits.</p>
                                <p>At-home LED devices are an excellent way to bring expensive in-clinic treatment to
                                    the comfort of your home for a fraction of the price. Remember, LED treatments
                                    deliver cumulative results, commitment is key. So this is why particularly at-home
                                    LED devices are worth your investment. They allow you to perform regular LED light
                                    therapy treatments on your skin at home, which means you’ll be able to see short
                                    term results and get long term benefits.</p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="wear_led_mask pt-30 pt-md-60">
                                <img src="assets/images/blogs/wear_led_mask.webp" alt=""
                                    class="img-fluid d-none d-md-block">
                                <img src="assets/images/blogs/wear_led_mask_mob.webp" alt=""
                                    class="img-fluid d-md-none">
                            </div>
                            <div class="led_safe_at_home pt-30 pt-md-60">
                                <p class="fs-24"><strong>Are At-Home LED devices safe?</strong></p>
                                <p>The testing for at-home devices is actually more rigorous than professional ones
                                    because the device is being cleared to use without the presence of a professional –
                                    there's a higher-level burden of proof to show efficacy and safety because a
                                    consumer is in charge of their own treatment.</p>
                                <p>An at-home device like the Q-Rejuvalight Pro Facewear is a seriously effective option
                                    to invest in.</p>
                                <p>Q-Rejuvalight Pro Facewear offers a three-minute treatment with a combination of 100
                                    red LED lights and 62 blue LED lights; is non-thermal and does not use UV light.
                                    It’s equipped with an automatic shut off feature, heat regulators and timer.</p>
                                <p>Unlike any other device on the market, the Q-Rejuvalight Pro Facewear comes with a
                                    compatible iOS/ Android app which allows you to totally customize every treatment
                                    according to your skin concerns. Whether it be programming red lights on your
                                    forehead and eye area whilst having blue lights on your chin and nose.</p>
                                <p>With a device like this, you are able to perform daily LED light therapy treatments,
                                    totally customized to your own skin, and get maximum benefits. It’s a certain way to
                                    transform your own skin without the trips to the salons and “clinical” price
                                    tags. and get long term benefits.</p>
